# The arms of a key that is told apart by its written names covered the one read: they met right behind it as any value, the sum was a generic operation outside arms, the try of the loop heard other code and no second build
# was bought; the store under the same key stayed as written. Now the arms run up to the last access under that key in the block: the read, the sum and the store are walked in each arm with the key known.
# RUN(HEADS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# HEADS-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# HEADS-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(STORES): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# STORES: PutSlot {{*}} key="price"
# STORES: PutSlot {{*}} key="stock"
